+  arcgym/heldout/_explorer.py    llm-oracle 9fdd3075          habit order, nearest rule, level-1 switch (XLW, 240)
+  arcgym/heldout/policies.py     llm-oracle 9fdd3075          _explore_fv(interleave=4, level1_only=True) = FL
+  arcgym/oracle/click_order.py   llm-oracle 9fdd3075          ClickOrder (FG + the level-1 drip)
+  arcgym/oracle/travel_repair.py llm-oracle 9fdd3075          TravelRepair (V)
+  arcgym/eca/primitive_synthesis._valued_components, arcgym/eca/button_click_prior.status_bar_cells (identical in
+  llm-oracle and fly-executor-r3; status_bar_cells is absent from the arcgym the ECA port ships, hence vendored here)
+Configuration (every FL measurement): RETRY_MAX=1, ORDER_MODE=dfs, DEADSITE=order, REACH_MODE=components, RESETSHORT=0,
+CARRY=0, CLEARDEAD=0, habit order on, nearest target rule on the first level after 240 actions without a level,
+ClickOrder("rank", gate=2, seed=20261001, interleave=4, interleave_level1_only=True), TravelRepair("traj").
+
+Driving it: `Level1Explorer(step, reset, budget=...).run(obs0)`. `step(engine_id, x, y)` executes ONE engine action
+(ids 1-6; x/y only for 6) and returns the new raw frame data (`.frame`, `.state`, `.levels_completed`,
+`.available_actions`); `reset()` executes a RESET and returns the same. Every step and every RESET is charged one
+action, as competition scoring charges them. The play stops at the budget, the time cap, `should_stop()`, or (with
+`stop_at_level_up`, the harness's use) right after the first action that raises the completed level count.
