+_EXPECT_DESCRIPTION_ANCHOR = "and `action(actions)` for executing one or more real environment actions. "
+_EXPECT_DESCRIPTION_NEW = (
+    "and `action(actions, expect=None)` for executing one or more real environment actions; `expect` is an optional "
+    "dict stating what you predict this call does - `changes` (bool: something changes inside the board area), `cells` "
+    "(list of [row, col] that will change), `level_up` (bool), `game_over` (bool) - or one such dict per action; the "
+    "harness compares it with what happened and returns EXPECTATION HELD or REFUTED in the output and in "
+    "`last_action_call_result['expectation']`. "
+)
+_EXPECT_TOOL_LINE_ANCHOR = "and `action(actions)`."
+_EXPECT_TOOL_LINE_NEW = "and `action(actions, expect=None)`."
+EXPECT_ADDENDUM = (
+    "- `action(actions, expect=...)` lets you state, before the actions run, what you predict they will do: "
+    "`{\"changes\": true}` (something inside the board area changes), `{\"cells\": [[row, col], ...]}` (those cells "
+    "change), `{\"level_up\": true}`, `{\"game_over\": false}`; combine keys freely, or pass one dict per action. "
+    "The harness compares the prediction with the actual transition and answers EXPECTATION HELD or EXPECTATION "
+    "REFUTED with what disagreed, in the snippet's output and in `last_action_call_result['expectation']`. State an "
+    "expectation on every call that acts: a refuted expectation means the rule you used for that action is wrong, so "
+    "change the rule before relying on it again; a held one is evidence for it. After several refutations in a row "
+    "on a level you will be reminded to rewrite the hypothesis.\n"
+)
